/target
# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored: this workspace ships binaries
# (ssk, sskd, ssk-svc). A tracked lockfile is what makes a build a
# reproducible statement and what makes `cargo audit` / `cargo deny`
# results refer to the versions we actually ship.
.env
*.log
*.tmp
# `sskd` writes its lock/state here when run from the repo root (see
# ssk-ipc::paths::state_dir). P2 moves the default off the CWD to %LOCALAPPDATA%;
# until then, keep the runtime artifact out of the working tree.
/.ssk
